  "id": "negative-incentive",
  "term": "negative incentive",
  "definition": "A negative incentive is a penalty-based influence on choice, where the possibility of losses for violating rules is used to encourage a desired behavior. In this context, raising the level of negative incentive increased workers’ decisions to reduce waste, although the added effect became smaller at higher levels.",
